        'description' => 'Summer 1945. The war is over. Two front-line friends, Mark Schwartz and Pyotr Ikonnikov, are in Hosta. Walking along the embankment, they meet a beautiful girl Tanya, who is looking after two twin girls, Englishwomen Sara and Beth. At this moment, neither Schwartz nor Ikonnikov yet suspects that a fleeting encounter will determine their entire future life. They do not yet know that the governess - Tanya Grazhdankina - serves in the MGB and is secretly in love with the girls\' father John Harper; that Harper - a double agent - will be exposed by the English and written off by Soviet intelligence to the GULAG as unnecessary; that Tanya will also end up in the camp and give birth to Harper\'s daughter, who will later take the funny nickname Nice; that Beth will become Pyotr\'s wife, and Sara will marry Mark; that both of them, having become artists, will build a common house in the village of Goncharovka, in which they will live together until after a quarrel they divide the house in half with a partition; that the English aristocrat John Harper will return to this house from the camp and end his life as a village shepherd; that Pyotr and Beth will adopt Nice, who awaits a truly bright and dramatic fate... The ups and downs of the artist friends, harmony and hatred between relatives, betrayal and fidelity of loving hearts, the heavy oppression and unexpected mercy of authoritarian power - the post-war Soviet history from 1945 to 1986 serves as the main catalyst for a non-trivial family saga, where from generation to generation of the Russian-English family a passionate attachment to Russia, frightening and beckoning, is passed down.'
    ],
    'долгий путь домой' => [
        'title' => 'Long Way Home',
        'year' => '2014',
        'type' => 'TV Series',
        'logline' => 'The story of two generations: from the early 80s to our days. Village girl Nadya falls in love with a metropolitan official and marries him. This marriage was not happy, Nadya dies prematurely when she realizes that she is not needed by her husband. Her daughter Lyalya will have to take a long way home – actually to herself.',
        'director' => 'Olga Dobrova-Kulikova',
        'screenwriter' => 'Tatyana Artseulova',
        'cinematographer' => 'Ivan Pomorin, Oleg Topoev',
        'composer' => 'Vladimir Davydenko',
        'production_designer' => 'Igor Kotsarev, Maria Fomina',
        'cast' => 'Darya Moroz, Elizaveta Boyarskaya, Alexander Lazarev Jr., Artem Tkachenko, Evgenia Brik, Natalia Surkova, Mikhail Evlanov, Yana Yesipovich, Miriam Sekhon',
        'episodes' => '16 episodes',
        'image' => 'images/dolpd.jpg',
        'description' => 'Nadya Chebotareva lives in the province. Everything in her life is simple and clear. Until a young handsome man, a promising official from Moscow – Vitaly Bolshakov – arrives in their village. Nadya falls in love and soon after his departure leaves her father\'s house and her fiancé Vitya to find her beloved in Moscow. She succeeds. But Vitaly turns out to be not at all the kind and friendly person he seemed to Nadya. However, he marries Nadya, because a marriage with a girl "from the people" comes in handy for his career at that moment. Vitaly and Nadya have a daughter Lyalya. The father dotes on his daughter, but this marriage cannot be called happy. Nadya understands that her husband does not love her, but she can\'t do anything about it. Her hopes for a happy life slowly but surely fade, and Nadya herself fades with them. Lyalya loves her mother, but does not understand her the same way as her father. Unable to endure the cynical behavior of Bolshakov\'s new lover, Nadya ends up in the hospital and dies. And Lyalya soon finds herself in a situation where her beloved father reveals his true face to her. Her father, by that time a major businessman playing a dishonest game, enters into a confrontation with Lyalya\'s husband Andrey, who serves as Bolshakov\'s chief economist. To get rid of the overly honest employee, Bolshakov arranges a car accident. Bolshakov is helped by his main partner, Yuri, who once was going to marry Lyalya and was unrequitedly in love with her. Lyalya leaves home. The only place on earth where she can go now is her mother\'s village house. There Lyalya finds peace of mind, and the son of her mother\'s former fiancé Viktor becomes her support. Lyalya understands that this is her real home. And how long was the way to it…'
    ],
    'за 5 минут до января' => [
        'title' => '5 Minutes Before January',
        'year' => '2017',
        'type' => 'TV Series',
        'logline' => 'On New Year\'s Eve, in snowy Babaevo, five absolutely different people from different social strata, with different fates, find themselves at once. Television brought them together to shoot a final report. Of course, New Year\'s miracles will grant each of the heroes the fulfillment of their most cherished dream.',
        'director' => 'Olga Dobrova-Kulikova',
        'screenwriter' => 'Maria Zvereva',
        'cinematographer' => 'Ivan Pomorin',
        'composer' => 'Vladimir Davydenko',
        'production_designer' => 'Vladislav Travinsky',
        'cast' => 'Dmitry Miller, Natalia Rudova, Evgenia Dobrovolskaya, Alexey Morozov, Alena Konstantinova',
        'episodes' => '4 episodes',
        'image' => 'images/za5minutdojanvar.jpg',
        'description' => 'Everyone knows that miracles happen on New Year\'s Eve. Television, generous with New Year\'s gifts, is especially interested in miracles. But nothing foreshadowed a truly fabulous plot twist when the General Producer of the General TV channel selected for the final report "5 Minutes Before January" five seemingly unrelated reports and five absolutely different heroes: the fashionable composer Savitsky, the brave rescuer, EMERCOM major Makarov, the capricious pop diva Elizaveta Barysheva, the beginning singer, the head of the children\'s music studio Olesya Tsvetkova and the summer resident-pensioner Petrovich from the village of Babaevo, who turned out to be a little bit of a wizard at the same time. A whirlwind of incredible events sweeps up each of these heroes. Their plans change radically in an instant and they all, by fair means or foul, suddenly find themselves in snowy Babaevo. Away from the city hustle and bustle on New Year\'s Eve, each of them will meet their happiness – to the delight of the entertainer Petrovich.'
    ],
    'ты меня слышишь' => [
        'title' => 'Do You Hear Me?',
        'year' => '2018',
        'type' => 'TV Series',
        'logline' => 'When Anna — the ideal wife of the ideal husband Sergey — gets into an accident, Sergey sees an intimate video on her phone. Who is it addressed to? He, in fact, is not without sin himself. Sergey tries to answer the question — when did the crack appear in their marriage? Who is to blame for this?',
        'director' => 'Nana Dzhordzhadze',
