        'cinematographer' => 'Mikhail Kvirikadze',
        'composer' => 'Dato Evgenidze',
        'production_designer' => 'Vladimir Salimov',
        'cast' => 'Victoria Isakova, Konstantin Lavronenko, Anna Starshenbaum, Alexander Baranovsky',
        'episodes' => '4 episodes',
        'image' => 'images/timenyaslishish.jpg',
        'description' => 'Sergey and Anna are the "ideal family". He is a successful architect, she is an artist who has become a housewife. Two children: Dimka is 15 years old and Dasha is 6. One day Anna gets into an accident. She is in a coma. In the hospital, Sergey is given her things. There is someone else\'s phone in her purse. Accidentally turning it on, Sergey sees an intimate video. Who did his wife pose for? Fury, confusion, jealousy and a sense of guilt, because Sergey himself is not without sin — he has an affair with a girl from a tattoo parlor. What went wrong in their marriage? Why did the ideal marriage end in disaster? Again and again, Sergey tries to talk to Anna, who is suspended between life and death. Will the former intimacy return?'
    ],
    'серебряный бор' => [
        'title' => 'Silver Pine Forest',
        'year' => '2017',
        'type' => 'TV Series',
        'logline' => 'The family saga covers the action from the late 70s to the early 80s. An elite Soviet family actually falls apart under the pressure of historical trials. The head of the family, General Arkhipov Sr., in order to save his family from trouble, is forced to fake his death.',
        'director' => 'Zinovy Roizman',
        'screenwriter' => 'Galina Salgarelli, Zinovy Roizman',
        'cinematographer' => 'Vitaly Konevtsov',
        'composer' => 'Evgeny Shiryayev',
        'production_designer' => 'Yuri Allenov, Vladimir Dushin',
        'cast' => 'Maria Shukshina, Sergey Makhovikov, Mikhail Pshenichny, Mark Bogatyrev, Nil Kropalov, Alina Lanina, Svetlana Smirnova-Katsagadzhieva, Anastasia Mikulchina, Vera Shpak',
        'episodes' => '24 episodes',
        'image' => 'images/sereb-bor.jpg',
        'description' => 'A family saga with elements of a detective story. Late 70s - early 80s. An elite Soviet family. Ivan Arkhipov is a Major General of the Ministry of Internal Affairs, a teacher at the Higher School of Militia, a former operative. His wife Tatyana Mikhailovna is an editor in a popular literary newspaper. Three adult sons: Pavel is an investigator at Petrovka, Alexey is an inspector of the district committee of the Komsomol, Kostya is finishing the history department of Moscow State University. A three-room apartment in the center of Moscow, a dacha in Serebryany Bor... Life has worked out! But historical events and personal confrontations become the most serious test for this family. Pavel is investigating a case of smuggling historical valuables abroad, the ends of which lead to high-ranking officials of the Central Committee. The idealist Arkhipov Sr. does not believe that corruption has penetrated the highest echelons of power, but still helps his son in the investigation, risking his official position and peace in the family. Alexey\'s romance with his boss Margarita is replaced by an affair with model Natasha, so his marriage to his childhood friend, the daughter of KGB General Alina, is falling apart. Kostya, to his father\'s spite, hastily marries an applicant of a theatrical university — the beauty Katya, and then just as hastily divorces her. Having broken with his father, he goes on an archaeological expedition to Altai, so Pavel takes care of Katya and her newborn child, who falls in love with his brother\'s ex-wife... Secrets, intrigues, understatement... The once close-knit family actually falls apart. Tatyana Mikhailovna, suspecting her husband of cheating and suffering from loneliness, responds to the courtship of her longtime admirer, film director Peskov... A turning point in the series is the death of Brezhnev, the arrest of Minister Shchelokov and the ensuing repression within the Ministry of Internal Affairs. Arkhipov refuses to give false testimony against his former boss, and, in order to save his loved ones from trouble, is forced to disappear, having faked his death. But it would be very difficult to outplay historical circumstances if it were not for the family — torn by time, but not ceased to be a family.'
    ],
    'служба доверия' => [
        'title' => 'Trust Service',
        'year' => '2007',
        'type' => 'TV Series',
        'logline' => 'The crisis "Trust Service" is ready to help people around the clock, return their faith in life, cope with the fear of loneliness, and alleviate mental pain.',
        'director' => 'Elena Nikolaeva',
        'screenwriter' => 'Natalia Chepik',
        'cinematographer' => 'Alexey Molchanov',
        'composer' => 'Alexey Garnizov',
        'production_designer' => 'Tatyana Devirts',
        'cast' => 'Tatyana Dogileva, Evgenia Simonova, Maria Shukshina, Georgy Tatarovkin, Inga Strelkova-Oboldina, Mikhail Politseimako, Alexandra Nazarova, Alexander Ratnikov, Semyon Morozov, Yana Sekste',
        'episodes' => '12 episodes',
        'image' => 'images/clujbadoveria.jpg',
        'description' => '"Trust Service" is a story about the most acute problems of modern life. The task of the series is to demonstrate that there is an opportunity to resolve these excruciating psychological, moral, and personal problems, that seemingly hopeless situations are not catastrophic. And special people will be able to help find a way out of the dead end. The series is about them and those who need their help. These special people work in the state crisis service and are ready to listen and help anyone who calls or comes for an appointment around the clock. They will help alleviate mental pain, relieve stress, revive the will to live, and cope with the fear of loneliness. Together with you, they will get to the bottom of the true causes of family conflicts and help resolve them. They are entrusted with the most secret intimate experiences, they are told about their complexes, which are familiar to every viewer, regardless of age, political climate, or the unstable dollar exchange rate... It is not by chance that this state crisis service is called the "Trust Service".'
    ],
