        'production_designer' => 'Igor Topilin',
        'cast' => 'Inna Makarova, Andrey Tolubeyev, Olga Ostroumova, Alexandra Florinskaya, Sergey Makhovikov, Oksana Akinshina, Elena Korikova, Andrey Chadov, Sergey Gorobchenko, Ekaterina Volkova, Stepan Morozov',
        'episodes' => '19 episodes',
        'duration' => '50 min',
        'image' => 'images/kapdeti.jpg',
        'description' => 'A contemporary melodrama based on the novels by Anna Berseneva "Captain\'s Children". At its heart are powerful emotions and fateful coincidences. The series takes place in our time. At the center of the film is a large Moscow family, the Grinyovs, representatives of its different generations, who experience unique yet equally captivating love stories. These are decent, reliable people, who possess a deeply hidden but very strong soulful responsiveness and innate nobility. Suggesting the right moves, sometimes intriguing, testing, deceiving, fate leads the heroes of the series through life. Over the three to four years during which we observe the Grinyovs, they become a little different, acquiring new character traits. Someone becomes wiser, someone — softer and more tolerant, and someone realizes that they are capable of taking responsibility for their loved ones, and finds happiness in this. Many events of the film unfold in unusual, sometimes even extreme circumstances. Here and the work of EMERCOM rescuers, and Chechen captivity, and the backstage life of television, and a luxurious foreign resort, and the Yakut diamond "kingdom", and the adventures of the hero and heroine who found themselves alone on a deserted ocean shore. New people rush into the Grinyovs\' lives along with conflicts, new stories begin. And their resolutions entail the next ones — even more amazing, but at the same time realistic plots.'
